 "readout_extra": [
  "<b>The interaction drop is a June artefact, not a July decline.</b> June logged 366 interactions, but 21 June alone accounted for 284 of them (273 likes from 268 accounts in a single day). Excluding that one day, June was 82 interactions and July's 146 is roughly 78% ahead on a like-for-like basis.",
  "<b>Partner and creator content drove the reach.</b> The three highest-reaching posts were all reshares: a Clay Health and Organics shelf tour (198 accounts reached), a Foodbank Victoria warehouse visit (194) and a Coeliac at Home cinnamon scroll reel (162). Owned brand posts peaked at 215. Reposting stockist and creator content is the cheapest reach lever available.",
  "<b>Facebook was the quiet winner:</b> 4,218 organic impressions, up 59% on June and the strongest month of the campaign, on 29 new page fans.",
  "<b>LinkedIn needs attention.</b> Impressions fell to 236 from 697 across five posts, returning one click and one new follower. The B2B track is not yet earning its place in the mix."
